<title>UK: High winds keep Black Sea Novorossiisk closed.</title>
<headline>High winds keep Black Sea Novorossiisk closed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading Russian Black Sea oil outlet Novorossiisk remained closed on Friday because of stormy weather, a reliable shipping source said.</p>
<p>The 700,000 barrel a day (bpd) terminal shut at 1300 local time on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Storm force winds on Friday were expected to moderate by the afternoon, the shipper said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
